    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1088">

                <pb facs="1013" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 351.622a/37</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The French Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jusserand</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 3, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Answering my recent
                    telegrams, my Government cables me that entirely trusting in the information
                    kindly supplied by the United States Government as to the inoffensive and
                    pacific character of the German subjects<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1088-f1"/>
                    recently arrested by the <hi rendition="#italic">Descartes</hi>, it has given
                    orders for their immediate release.</p>
                <p>They will be placed under the care of the American Consul at Fort de France.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jusserand</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1088-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1088-f1-content">
                <p>By another letter of the same day, the word “individuals” was substituted for
                    “German subjects,” thereby including also the Austrians (File No.
                    351.622a/27).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
